{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates a reasonable structural understanding of EDIFACT message hierarchy but suffers from critical flattening errors, missing qualifier distinctions, and incomplete segment coverage. The model captures only ~20% of required D96A INVOIC segments and conflates semantically distinct EDIFACT concepts (e.g., all NAD segments, all date types). Cardinality rules are underspecified, and mandatory EANCOM business constraints are absent.",
  "completeness_score": 0.23,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTMSegment with qualifier subclasses (DTM+137, DTM+35, DTM+11)",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "The ontology has :hasDocumentDate as a data property on HeaderSection, but D96A requires explicit DTM segments with qualifiers. DTM+137 (Document Date) is MANDATORY in EANCOM INVOIC. DTM+35 (Delivery Date) and DTM+11 (", "owl_reviewed_length": 18138, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 1}

