{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates sophisticated OWL modeling with comprehensive inverse properties and reification patterns, but it suffers from critical EDIFACT semantic loss. The model abstracts away essential D96A EANCOM distinctions—treating all NAD segments generically, omitting qualifier-based semantics (DTM+137 vs DTM+35), and missing ~70% of mandatory INVOIC segments. The 'RoleAssignment' reification is architecturally sound but cannot compensate for the absence of segment-level EDIFACT constraints.",
  "completeness_score": 0.25,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTMSegment with qualifier-based subclasses (DTM+137 DocumentDate, DTM+35 DeliveryDate, DTM+11 DespatchDate)",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "D96A INVOIC mandates DTM+137 (Document Date) as Mandatory. Your :hasDocumentDate datatype property on :Header", "owl_reviewed_length": 20420, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 0}

